#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# squared_euclidean_distance

#% text
# `squared_euclidean_distance(u, v)` gives the sum of the |u_i - v_i|^2 for vectors u and v, the square of `euclidean_distance(u, v)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
squared_euclidean_distance([1, 5, 2], [4, 1, 0])
#% output
#= 29

#% cell
squared_euclidean_distance([a, b], [x, y])
#% output
#= abs(a - x)^2 + abs(b - y)^2

#% cell
squared_euclidean_distance([1, 2, 3], [0, 5/2, 2]) == euclidean_distance([1, 2, 3], [0, 5/2, 2])^2
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `euclidean_distance`, `manhattan_distance`
